session scratchpad task191-4/out):
- Plain same-host click: notRouted(sameHost), navigated in place.
- Plain cross-host click to localhost: routable(crossHostClick) ->
  openInSpace(Work) -> openInWindow(B); B came forward with the tab selected;
  A's tab stayed on its page (capture 02-cross-B/A).
- Cmd+click cross host: routable(commandClick) -> Work window B. Cmd+click
  same host (no route): routable, decision none -> background tab in A.
- target=_blank same host, path routed (kind=blank-work): routable(blankTarget)
  -> Work window (capture R4). _blank unrouted: a new tab here; its
  createWebViewWith call logs decidedByNavigationPolicy.
- window.open tab-style to localhost: routable(scriptedWindow) -> Work window.
  Popup-style: notRouted(popupWindow), a tab here, opener kept (the opener
  received the popup's postMessage).
- Option-click: the policy's Option branch runs before routing is asked; a
  split formed. Shift-click: Peek, routing not asked. In the Peek: a _blank
  link and a cross-host click to a Private-routed URL both notRouted(inPeek);
  the _blank opened a tab here as before, the click navigated the Peek.
- Server redirect (same-host link, 302 to localhost): sameHost, then the
  redirect asked again as link activation with _isRedirect=true ->
  notRouted(redirect); the tab ended on the redirect target. Client redirect
  (location.replace): notLinkActivation. onclick location.href:
  notLinkActivation with gesture=true. Page timer a.click(): noUserGesture.
  onclick a.click(): gesture=true, routed to Work (indistinguishable from a
  click, by design).
- Cross host with no route ([::1]): routable, decision none, in place.
- Pinned tab: cross-host click to localhost routed to Work, no Peek
  (16a); to [::1] (no route): Peek as before (16b); a same-host link that
  server-redirects to localhost: not routed, and the anchor intercept PEEKED
  the redirect target (16c) - pre-existing, WebKit reports the redirect as a
  link activation.
- Cmd+T "localhost:8714/b?kind=typed": routable, Work -> window B (17).
  Cmd+L: navigatesInPlace=true, not routable, loaded in A's tab. Search
  "routeme please": isSearch=true, not routable, a Google tab here (the one
  request outside the fixture).
- Private route from A with no Private window: openInNewPrivateWindow (20);
  again: openInPrivateWindow(P). From P, a cross-host click to localhost
  (Work route): routable, decision none, navigated in place (22). Typed in P:
  routable, decision none, a tab in P.
- Reruns (cmd-1b/1c below): the first plain click after a window became key
  sometimes did not land (no navigation action at all); re-posting it worked.

--- fixture/server.py ---
    # TASK-191.4 fixture server: a page of links, a target page, server and client
    # redirects. Bound to 127.0.0.1; pages reach it as 127.0.0.1 and as localhost
    # (two hosts for the cross-host rule). Logs every request to stdout.
    import sys, html
    from http.server import ThreadingHTTPServer, BaseHTTPRequestHandler
    from urllib.parse import urlparse, parse_qs

    PORT = int(sys.argv[1]) if len(sys.argv) > 1 else 8714

    LINKS = """<!doctype html><html><head><title>Links {tag}</title>
    <style>body{{font:15px -apple-system;margin:16px}} a,button{{display:block;margin:6px 0;font-size:15px;padding:4px}}</style></head>
    <body><h3>Links on {host} ({tag})</h3>
    <a id="same" href="/b?from={tag}&kind=same">same host /b</a>
    <a id="cross" href="http://{other}:{port}/b?from={tag}&kind=cross">cross host {other}/b</a>
    <a id="crosslinks" href="http://{other}:{port}/a?tag=peeked">cross host links page on {other}</a>
    <a id="v6" href="http://[::1]:{port}/b?from={tag}&kind=v6">cross host [::1]/b (no route)</a>
    <a id="crosspriv" href="http://{other}:{port}/b?from={tag}&kind=secret">cross host {other}/b secret</a>
    <a id="blank" target="_blank" href="http://{host}:{port}/b?from={tag}&kind=blank-work">_blank same host, work path</a>
    <a id="blankplain" target="_blank" href="http://{host}:{port}/b?from={tag}&kind=blank-plain">_blank same host, unrouted</a>
    <a id="sameWork" href="/b?from={tag}&kind=work">same host, work path (plain)</a>
    <a id="redir" href="/redir?to=http://{other}:{port}/b%3Ffrom%3D{tag}%26kind%3Dredirect">same host link, server redirect to {other}</a>
    <a id="clientredir" href="/clientredir?to=http://{other}:{port}/b%3Ffrom%3D{tag}%26kind%3Dclientredirect">same host link, client redirect to {other}</a>
    <button id="open" onclick="window.open('http://{other}:{port}/b?from={tag}&kind=open-tab')">window.open tab-style</button>
    <button id="popup" onclick="window.popupRef = window.open('http://{other}:{port}/popup?from={tag}&kind=open-popup', 'p', 'popup,width=420,height=320')">window.open popup-style</button>
    <button id="scriptnav" onclick="location.href='http://{other}:{port}/b?from={tag}&kind=scriptnav'">onclick location.href</button>
    <button id="scriptclick" onclick="setTimeout(()=>document.getElementById('cross').click(), 0)">onclick a.click()</button>
    <div id="received"></div>
    <script>
    window.received = [];
    window.addEventListener('message', e => {{ window.received.push(e.data); document.getElementById('received').textContent = 'popup said: ' + JSON.stringify(e.data); }});
    const auto = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('auto');
    if (auto === 'click') setTimeout(() => document.getElementById('cross').click(), 1200);
    if (auto === 'nav') setTimeout(() => {{ location.href = 'http://{other}:{port}/b?from={tag}&kind=timernav'; }}, 1200);
    </script></body></html>"""

    PAGE = """<!doctype html><html><head><title>B {kind} on {host}</title></head>
    <body style="font:15px -apple-system;margin:16px"><h3>Target B on {host}</h3><p>kind={kind} from={frm}</p>
    <a id="back" href="http://{host}:{port}/a?tag=b">links page</a></body></html>"""

    POPUP = """<!doctype html><html><head><title>Popup on {host}</title></head><body>
    <p>popup, opener={{}}</p><script>
    document.querySelector('p').textContent = 'popup, hasOpener=' + !!window.opener;
    if (window.opener) window.opener.postMessage({{ fromPopup: true }}, '*');
    </script></body></html>"""

    CLIENT = """<!doctype html><html><head><title>client redirect</title></head><body>
    <script>location.replace({to!r});</script></body></html>"""


    class H(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):
        def log_message(self, fmt, *args):
            sys.stdout.write("REQ %s %s\n" % (self.headers.get('Host'), self.path))
            sys.stdout.flush()

        def send_page(self, body, code=200):
            data = body.encode()
            self.send_response(code)
            self.send_header('Content-Type', 'text/html; charset=utf-8')
            self.send_header('Content-Length', str(len(data)))
            self.send_header('Cache-Control', 'no-store')
            self.end_headers()
            self.wfile.write(data)

        def do_GET(self):
            u = urlparse(self.path)
            q = {k: v[0] for k, v in parse_qs(u.query).items()}
            hosthdr = self.headers.get('Host') or '127.0.0.1'
            host = hosthdr[:hosthdr.index(']') + 1] if hosthdr.startswith('[') else hosthdr.split(':')[0]
            other = 'localhost' if host == '127.0.0.1' else '127.0.0.1'
            if u.path == '/a':
                self.send_page(LINKS.format(tag=html.escape(q.get('tag', 'a')), host=host, other=other, port=PORT))
            elif u.path == '/b':
                self.send_page(PAGE.format(kind=html.escape(q.get('kind', '')), frm=html.escape(q.get('from', '')), host=host, port=PORT))
            elif u.path == '/popup':
                self.send_page(POPUP.format(host=host))
            elif u.path == '/redir':
                self.send_response(302)
                self.send_header('Location', q.get('to', '/b'))
                self.send_header('Content-Length', '0')
                self.end_headers()
            elif u.path == '/clientredir':
                self.send_page(CLIENT.format(to=q.get('to', '/b')))
            else:
                self.send_page('not found', 404)


    import socket
    if len(sys.argv) > 2 and sys.argv[2] == 'v6':
        class V6(ThreadingHTTPServer):
            address_family = socket.AF_INET6
        V6(('::1', PORT), H).serve_forever()
    else:
        ThreadingHTTPServer(('127.0.0.1', PORT), H).serve_forever()

--- watch-captures.sh ---
    #!/bin/bash
    # Takes a window capture for every "CAPTURE <label> <windowNumber>" line the harness logs.
    OUT=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tma-Projects-browser-MyBrowser/20483124-f109-4f1c-ac33-b193eaf9d147/scratchpad/task191-4/out
    LOG=$OUT/verify-1.log
    seen=$(grep -c " CAPTURE " "$LOG" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)
    while true; do
      if [ -f "$LOG" ]; then
        n=$(grep -c " CAPTURE " "$LOG")
        if [ "$n" -gt "$seen" ]; then
          grep " CAPTURE " "$LOG" | tail -n +$((seen + 1)) | sed -E "s/.* CAPTURE //" | while read -r label num; do
            /usr/sbin/screencapture -x -o -l "$num" "$OUT/$label.png" && echo "captured $label ($num)"
          done
          seen=$n
        fi
        grep -q "STATE ${1:-end}:" "$LOG" && exit 0
      fi
      sleep 0.5
    done

